<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Achieng invests Ksh <m>{35\,000}</m> at <m>{9}\%</m> per annum compound interest, added at the end of each year.</p><p>(a) Find the amount after <m>{3}</m> years, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the compound interest earned.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>With compound interest, interest is added to the account, and next year's interest is paid on the bigger sum. Each year the amount is multiplied by <m>1 + \frac{ {9} }{100} = {1.09}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>A = P\left(1 + \dfrac{r}{100}\right)^n = {35\,000} \times {1.09}^{ {3} } = {45\,326.02}</m>, so the amount is Ksh <m>{45\,326}</m> to the nearest shilling. Round only at the end.</p><p>(b) Compound interest <m>= A - P = {45\,326.02} - {35\,000} = {10\,326.02}</m>, about Ksh <m>{10\,326}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>45326</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10326</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>